FINISHING YOUR CALL

A - Finishing your call

:A
FINISHING YOUR CALL

Finish any file transfer or draft message and leave the program you're using
in its normal fashion. From RBBS, C returns to CP/M; G logs off directly.

At the CP/M prompt enter:

    BYE

That ends your call and leaves the machine available for the next caller. You
can also disconnect with your terminal, but the ordinary logoff command is
preferable when circumstances permit.

WORK is cleared at call boundaries. Saved RBBS messages and your board account
remain, as do completed uploads and saved MESSAGE notes. The mounted library
volumes need not return to their defaults until the machine restarts or
somebody selects another volume.
